A||N||7||Black88GT||Amp in front compartment *questions*....||||5||
Z||000000||Black88GT||09-20-2000||05:39 PM||||With my last fiero I put the amp in the trunk.  I didn't like it at all.  This time around I want to build an enclosure that covers the front compartment and mount an amp in it, like this<P>------      -------  &lt;--covering top     <BR>      |_AMP_|||152.163.195.199||reg||5
Z||000001||Seanh||09-20-2000||09:30 PM||||Interesting, I have a subbox up there, and amps in the trunk. I ran the wires to the batt. through a subbox (no sub using this) port tube to the trunk. I believe you will have to drill some sort of hole to run the wires up there, I would do it right underneath the huge plug the goes up there on the drivers side front firewall. You could run there under the car, but youd still have to drill a hole. My batt has the postes on top and the GM side posts, so I used the top ones to run my system. If yours has that, just run a heavy guage wire from the top post and into the car, right behind the pass. seat and under the carpet and through the pass. side trim planels to the dash, over, and then out to the amp.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula||09-20-2000||10:35 PM||||theres a hole above the gas pedal that runs up into there through a grommet (yes I said grommet LOL).  as for drilling a hole, the only hole I had to drill was above the ecm to run my #8 power and ground wires.<P>also remember, the longer your speaker wire is the thicker it should be.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||09-21-2000||02:12 AM||||drilled a hole in the far right corner under dash for an 8 gauge cable for pos. lead. neg grounded in front trunk. useda big twist and lock type plug for 3 phase power so i could disconnect it and take the amp package out whe i need to. speaker and remote wires are in a plug on drivers side under dash. found a military type (that's where i've always seen them any way) cannon plug that i can disconnect. used some "through wall" rca plugs so i didn't have to run rca's from the dash to the amps (x over actually). again, it lets me disconnect them to get to my spare or just take my amp pack out.<P>i think a couple of those ideas are making my system a little noisier than it would be if every thing was wired strait though. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||09-21-2000||03:12 PM||||I think I can get away with running the RCAs and the speaker wire through the "grommet" where the gas pedal is, then running the power cable under the car up into the battery tray, being careful to keep it away from anything that gets hot.  Then I wouldn't need to cut any holes.  I may need to take the spare out, I havent decided yet. <P>This may sound stupid, but what if I put another battery up front.  I could put it where the spare tire is.  I would still have to run a battery cable to the main battery though right?<P>hmm..........<BR>thanks to those who have replied already<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||5
Z||000005||Seanh||09-21-2000||05:53 PM||||Thats what I have. One batt. in the modified stock location (had to be made deeper for this batt.) and one upfront. Check out <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com</A>   he has some batt. relocation trays that look nice up front, and can be used under the spare batt. And Yes, you would have to run wires from you existing batt. to the second to allow it to charge. My second batt. is sitting where the widow washer fluid tank used to be.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Black88GT||09-21-2000||10:25 PM||||I would love to take out the windshield washer fluid tank and cut holes to easily run the wires through, but I always think that I will regret it.  I don't want to go to wild, I know its highly unlikely but it may become a collector one day and I might kick myself for cutting it up.  It is a factory t-top GT with beechwood interior, gold wheels and 5 speed.  I am not trying to brag or use the ole "my fiero is better then yours" mentality, but I just want to let you know where I am coming from.  I guess using a second battery would be useless since I would have to run the wires anyway, which I was trying to avoid.  If I was doing a serious system with 5 amps and crossovers etc. I would probably do the second battery.  I am only using (for now anyway) one 200 watt amp.  If I had the money I would buy the kit to move the battery up front to save me a lot of hassle!  I'll keep everyone updated on how I do.  I will post pics if and when I finish.<P>      <P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000007||Seanh||09-22-2000||07:39 AM||||I hear ya, not wanting to cut the car up. I felt the same way, but everthng I have done is removable and eaisly fixable. The only problem I might have is the pass. side port tube into the car.||||reg||1
